50
00:01:49.654 --> 00:01:51.874
One will need to produce a sound originating from

51
00:01:51.914 --> 00:01:53.025
the posterior pharynx.

52
00:01:53.055 --> 00:01:55.225
Like a bee or a bumblebee ascending,

53
00:01:55.265 --> 00:01:57.715
and this sound must rise into the cavity to

54
00:01:57.745 --> 00:01:59.683
culminate at the level of the sinuses.

55
00:01:59.824 --> 00:02:02.234
We will assess the entire cerebral region,

56
00:02:02.274 --> 00:02:05.427
extending into the tympanic cavity and sinus cavity.

57
00:02:06.052 --> 00:02:09.232
Frontal, sphenoidal, maxillary, and even temporal.

58
00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:11.367
We will first adopt an upright posture.

59
00:02:11.444 --> 00:02:14.234
When I straighten my back, upon exhalation,

60
00:02:14.274 --> 00:02:16.804
I will experience the true physiological effect

61
00:02:16.904 --> 00:02:19.144
of a release on my vagal tone.

62
00:02:19.917 --> 00:02:22.427
this parasympathetic and restorative system.

63
00:02:22.457 --> 00:02:25.157
If I position myself thus, and restrict here,

64
00:02:25.197 --> 00:02:26.686
I diminish this capacity.

65
00:02:26.895 --> 00:02:30.085
I experience this state of inspiratory awareness.

66
00:02:30.795 --> 00:02:34.345
Second level, I am very, very attentive to the act

67
00:02:34.385 --> 00:02:34.805
of

68
00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:36.825
respiration.

69
00:02:36.935 --> 00:02:40.365
I am aware of the body's movement during the

70
00:02:40.405 --> 00:02:41.475
respiratory act.

71
00:02:41.505 --> 00:02:42.730
Fourth level, I relax.

72
00:02:42.935 --> 00:02:46.235
upon exhalation, fully conscious that I am inhaling.

73
00:02:46.339 --> 00:02:48.387
We will perform twelve respirations.

74
00:02:48.426 --> 00:02:50.516
the first two we will perform thus,

75
00:02:50.556 --> 00:02:52.886
and the last ten we will perform with the

76
00:02:53.046 --> 00:02:56.026
ears slightly occluded; you will place your fingers

77
00:02:56.066 --> 00:02:56.906
over your ears

78
00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:59.320
to facilitate internal integration;

79
00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.080
you inhale, and during the

80
00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:03.486
expiratory phase, you produce a gentle humming

81
00:03:03.526 --> 00:03:03.876
sound.

82
00:03:13.066 --> 00:03:16.276
we inhale, occlude the ears, and you perform this

83
00:03:16.497 --> 00:03:19.147
ten times, and then you may release; you

84
00:03:22.677 --> 00:03:24.887
enter into the emerging silence,

85
00:03:24.927 --> 00:03:26.627
and within this silence, you

86
00:03:26.777 --> 00:03:29.947
simply allow a feeling of joy to arise, and

87
00:03:32.197 --> 00:03:34.807
if you are unsure what to do, offer a small

88
00:03:34.837 --> 00:03:37.647
smile; take another inhalation, perform

89
00:03:41.068 --> 00:03:44.098
an exhalation, and at the conclusion of the

90
00:03:44.138 --> 00:03:44.858
exhalation,

91
00:03:44.888 --> 00:03:47.538
There is a space where you do not respire.

92
00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:50.940
But you settle your consciousness within this space.

93
00:03:52.848 --> 00:03:55.920
Even as you reinspire, you remain within this space.

94
00:03:56.868 --> 00:03:59.528
When you enter this perception, you bring yourself

95
00:03:59.568 --> 00:04:00.138
closer

96
00:04:02.288 --> 00:04:03.728
to the embryonic breath.

97
00:04:05.368 --> 00:04:07.878
Because the embryonic breath was not subject to

98
00:04:07.918 --> 00:04:09.658
